      "body": "Closes #10385\n\nBefore: the GitHub hot-list consumer test \"generated failure/restart schedules never checkpoint undurable rows or duplicate activity\" failed now and then on a busy machine, stopping partway with fewer expect() calls than a passing run.\n\nAfter: the test has a 60s limit, like the repo's other heavy tests, and passes on a busy machine.\n\nThe schedules are not random: the 48 seeds are fixed, so every run checks the same traces. The failures were bun's default 5s per-test timeout. The test runs in about 0.5s on an idle host and about 1s with every core busy, but run niced under heavy CPU contention it reports \"this test timed out after 5000ms\" and stops partway through the seeds, which matches the short expect() count in the issue. No consumer bug is involved.\n\nHow: an explicit `60_000` timeout on that one test, with a comment saying why. Ran the file idle (15 pass) and under load (15 pass), and 40 parallel runs of the file (all pass).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01YLT5JyFdZgVpkFFqSHMPHV)_\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://dashboardbackend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1797594455&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=11792&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F11792&signature=e9d056cc7e0ff2745be661f32c6535f17fcd034689b4cc426b2a8ac85b8c1095\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/co